# ── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# ── Build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# `api/index.js` is DELIBERATELY NOT ignored — do not add it back.
#
# It is built by `pnpm build:api` (scripts/build-server.mjs) as a SELF-CONTAINED
# bundle of the whole server, and it is the function that serves /trpc, /api and
# /app-storage (see the rewrites in vercel.json). `dist/` stays ignored because
# Vercel rebuilds it from source and the SPA there is a pure build output.
#
# This file is different: its build runs NO typecheck or tests, so a broken
# server reaches it silently, and this pre-bundled artifact is exactly what the
# nft-dependent deploy needs (see the long note in scripts/build-server.mjs).
# Committing it keeps the artifact that actually ships in the diff.
#
# History: commit a562f5d added `api/index.js` here, which removed the function
# from the repository. Every /api and /trpc request then fell through to the SPA
# rewrite and received `/index.html` — the API was gone in production, and
# sign-in died with `Unexpected token 'T', "The page c"...` because the client
# parsed that HTML page as JSON. Keep this file tracked.

